# TASK
Build a complete, runnable, production-quality React landing page for a fictional travel brand called NOMIRA. This is a real frontend project (not a mockup, not pseudo-code, not a description). Deliver every file needed to run `npm install && npm run dev` and deploy to Vercel with `npm run build`.

The attached screenshot is the primary visual reference. It is a desktop design downscaled to ~402px wide, so reproduce its COMPOSITION, PROPORTIONS, HIERARCHY and MOOD at real desktop size, and adapt intentionally for tablet and mobile. Do not copy the screenshot's tiny type or force four cramped columns onto a phone.

Design character: premium, minimal, editorial, cinematic travel. Neutral UI, colour comes from photography. It must NOT look like a generic SaaS/travel template: no random gradients, no glassmorphism cards everywhere, no heavy shadows, no oversized rounded boxes, no decorative blobs. The only translucent/blurred elements are the nav capsule and the hero search bar, as in the reference.

# TECH STACK (fixed)
- React + Vite (JavaScript or TypeScript, your choice, be consistent), Tailwind CSS (use the stable version you can scaffold reliably; define design tokens in the Tailwind theme), CSS Grid/Flexbox.
- GSAP (+ ScrollTrigger) for subtle reveals only.
- lucide-react for generic UI icons. Brand/social icons and the NOMIRA logo mark must be inline SVG components.
- Aceternity UI: OPTIONAL, at most two components, only where one genuinely matches the reference. If it would add unreliable dependencies, skip it and build with Tailwind + GSAP. Never use Aceternity decorative backgrounds (aurora, sparkles, beams, spotlight). If an Aceternity component forces the `motion` package, use it only inside that component and nowhere else.
- No Next.js, Bootstrap, Material UI, backend, auth, analytics, paid APIs, or booking infrastructure. No secrets in source.
- "No frameworks" is resolved as: only the stack above and nothing else heavy.

# TYPOGRAPHY
- Primary (display): Bricolage Grotesque, for hero heading, all section headings, brand statement, statistics numbers, card titles, footer wordmark.
- Secondary: Poppins, for body copy, nav, buttons, form controls, labels, metadata, captions, pills.
- Load via Google Fonts in index.html with preconnect and display=swap:
  Bricolage Grotesque with opsz and wght axes (opsz 12..96, wght 200..800) and Poppins 300;400;500;600.
- Tailwind: fontFamily.display = Bricolage Grotesque, fontFamily.sans = Poppins; body defaults to Poppins. Set font-optical-sizing:auto on display text.
- Headings: weight 400-500 (the reference looks light/regular, not bold), line-height 0.95-1.1, letter-spacing about -0.02em. Statistic numbers weight 500.
- Fluid scale with clamp():
  - Hero H1: clamp(2.75rem, 7.2vw, 6rem)
  - Section H2: clamp(2rem, 3.8vw, 3.5rem)
  - Brand statement: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 4.5rem)
  - Stat number: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.5rem)
  - Card title: clamp(1.05rem, 1.3vw, 1.35rem)
  - Body: 0.9375-1rem, small/meta: 0.75-0.8125rem. Never go below 12px on any screen.

