# DATA AND CODE ORGANISATION
- Keep content in structured arrays under src/data/: trips, destinations, stories, faqs, stats, navLinks, footerLinks, images. Components map over data; no duplicated markup.
- Suggested structure:
  src/
    main.jsx / App.jsx
    index.css (Tailwind layers, tokens, font settings, reduced-motion rules, scrollbar-hiding utilities)
    data/ (trips, destinations, stories, faqs, stats, navigation, images)
    components/
      layout/ Header, MobileMenu, Footer
      sections/ HeroSection, TripSearch, PopularTrips, BrandStatement, StatisticsSection, DestinationExplorer, TravelerStories, FAQSection, PromotionalCTA
      ui/ Button, Chip, Accordion, Dialog, Pager, SectionHeading, TicketCard, PolaroidCard, SmartImage, Logo, SocialIcon
    hooks/ useReveal (GSAP ScrollTrigger wrapper), useScrollCarousel, useActiveSection, useReducedMotion
- Semantic structure: <header>, <main>, <section aria-labelledby>, <footer>, <nav aria-label>. One <h1> (hero), <h2> per section, <h3> for card titles. Meaningful class names via Tailwind composition; no giant unreadable class strings repeated, extract components.
- No empty handlers, no TODOs, no missing imports, no console errors or warnings.

# IMAGES
- Central registry src/data/images.js exporting an object keyed by id. Each entry: { src, alt, objectPosition, width, height, fallback } where fallback is a tasteful CSS gradient matched to the photo's palette.
- Use direct, stable image URLs (e.g. images.unsplash.com photo URLs with ?auto=format&fit=crop&w=...&q=80 and sensible srcSet/sizes). Only use photo IDs you are confident exist and that match the subject; do NOT use random-image or search endpoints (no source.unsplash.com, no picsum for travel subjects). Make it trivial to swap every image later by editing the registry.
- Required subjects: hero (hot-air balloons, rocky dusk landscape); Bali surfer on a beach with palms; Cappadocia balloons over valley; Tokyo busy street with signage; Raja Ampat lagoon islands (aerial turquoise); dark teal aerial ocean with tiny swimmers/boats; Santorini white-and-blue domes at sunset; Kyoto pagoda street; Palawan limestone cliffs lagoon; extra destination photos; 5 candid traveller portraits; 4 small avatar portraits; Fuji-like mountain sunset.
- <SmartImage> component: object-fit cover with per-image object-position; explicit width/height or aspect-ratio box (prevents layout shift); loading="lazy" and decoding="async" for everything below the fold, eager + fetchpriority="high" only for the hero; onError swaps to the gradient fallback (no broken-image icons, no black rectangles); meaningful alt for informational images, alt="" for decorative.
- Photos must correspond to the card content, no mismatched imagery.

# INTERACTION AND MOTION
- Everything that looks clickable must work: nav anchors with smooth scroll (CSS scroll-behavior with scroll-margin-top for the fixed header), mobile menu, search popovers and submit, Book Now / Book My Trip Now demo dialog, trip and destination carousels (buttons, dots, swipe, keyboard), destination filters, story button, FAQ accordion, newsletter form, footer links, Sign up dialog.
- Dialogs: accessible (role="dialog", aria-modal, labelled, focus trap, Escape to close, return focus, scroll lock).
- GSAP: subtle only: section heading and card fade/translate-up (about 16-24px, 0.5-0.7s, ease power2.out, staggered 0.06-0.1s), stat count-up, mild hover transitions via CSS. No parallax, no looping motion, no per-letter text animation, no cursor effects.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion everywhere (skip GSAP animations, set content to final visible state, disable transforms/transitions). Content must be visible even if JS animations fail (never leave elements stuck at opacity 0).

